course: dictionary
lesson: 2704
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Digging can mean making a hole in the ground or moving earth, with a spade, hands, paws or a machine. It can also mean searching hard for something, as in «digging for information». Read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: «In the North the Elephant's diggings become the Himalayas.» The story tells you that the land changes, so diggings must mean the places where earth has been dug up and moved. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «A real pig walks on four legs... and its flat snout is a strong, sensitive digging tool for roots and worms.» The clues are roots, worms and tool. Here digging means moving earth to find food. Digging is the -ing form of dig, so you will also see dig, digs and dug in other sentences.
fact: Digging is the -ing form of the verb dig.
fact: The other forms are dig, digs and dug, so «She dug a hole yesterday» uses the past form.
fact: «Digging» can mean making a hole in the ground or moving earth, with a spade, hands, paws or a machine.
fact: «Digging» can also mean searching hard for something, as in «digging for information».
fact: Safety tip: never dig deep holes in sand or near gas pipes, because sand holes can collapse.
exercise: Dad is digging in the garden to plant beans. What does digging mean here? | *Making a hole or moving soil with a spade | Painting a fence | Searching hard for lost keys | Sleeping under a tree
exercise: Priya spent the afternoon digging for information about the Sahara. What does digging mean here? | Swimming in a warm pool | Making a hole in the sand | *Searching hard for something
exercise: Which word is the -ing form of dig? | dug | dig | *digging | digs
test: Which word fits? «Dad is ___ a hole for the new tree.» | flying | singing | *digging | sleeping
test: What is a diggings? | A tool for cutting paper | A kind of sandwich | *Places where things have been dug up | A type of bird
exam: Read: «The pig's snout is a strong, sensitive digging tool for roots and worms.» Which meaning of digging fits best? | Searching the internet for facts | *Moving earth to find roots and worms | Dancing across the field
